{"caseId":"OD2-DEV-INCOMPLETE","answers":[{"itemId":"Q01","answer":"unknown","confidence":55,"evidenceIds":["E3","E5","X1","X6"]},{"itemId":"Q02","answer":"unknown","confidence":55,"evidenceIds":["E3","X6","X1"]},{"itemId":"Q03","answer":"contradicted","confidence":90,"evidenceIds":["X3","X14"]},{"itemId":"Q04","answer":"contradicted","confidence":88,"evidenceIds":["X14"]},{"itemId":"Q05","answer":"contradicted","confidence":92,"evidenceIds":["X2","E4"]},{"itemId":"Q06","answer":"association-only","confidence":60,"evidenceIds":["E3","E5","X14","X1"]},{"itemId":"Q07","answer":"association-only","confidence":60,"evidenceIds":["E3","X6","X14"]},{"itemId":"Q08","answer":"contradicted","confidence":88,"evidenceIds":["X14"]},{"itemId":"Q09","answer":"contradicted","confidence":88,"evidenceIds":["X3"]},{"itemId":"Q10","answer":"preferred","confidence":75,"evidenceIds":["X6","E3","X1"]},{"itemId":"Q11","answer":"premature","confidence":55,"evidenceIds":["E3","X1","X6"]},{"itemId":"Q12","answer":"premature","confidence":60,"evidenceIds":["X6","E3"]},{"itemId":"Q13","answer":"harmful","confidence":93,"evidenceIds":["X2","E4"]},{"itemId":"Q14","answer":"harmful","confidence":85,"evidenceIds":["X3","X14"]},{"itemId":"Q15","answer":"insufficient","confidence":75,"evidenceIds":["X6","X1","E3"]}],"brief":"The rise in missed appointments at Corrie Lane is real. It is not mainly a recording artefact: an audit found miscoding explains only about 0.5 points of the 13.4%. It is not the bus change or the season either. Eastgate, which shares the catchment and the bus route, stayed at about 8%, and Corrie Lane was about 8% a year earlier. Front-desk confirmation calls did not stop. Calls to the minor-procedures list were 93% before and 91% after, so the staff warnings should not go ahead. Hiding the figure from the board would also be a mistake.

The cause is almost certainly the Tidewell configuration. Two changes happened together on 3 March across all templates: the near-date reminder was replaced by a 7-day one, and booking lead times went from a median of about 19 days to about 52. Nothing in the data separates the two, and lead-time outcomes can't be extracted for about 10 weeks. I'm fairly sure of the rest and unsure which of these two matters more.

Next step: run the randomised 8-week test of a 48-hour reminder on half the templates, and ask the vendor for the booking-timestamp extract now. Don't change the booking horizon or the whole clinic's configuration until the test reports."}
